    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings until the Padres broke open the seventh.",
    "what_this_means": "King held San Francisco to three runs over seven innings, and the lineup converted at the right moments to steal a 7-6 win. Bogaerts went 4-for-5 and Tatis hit a solo shot. They did the work that mattered. But this wasn't dominance. It was opportunism in a game that could have folded twice. The sixth inning came and went empty, the ninth inning even emptier with runners in scoring position and nowhere to go. They had 13 hits and scored seven runs. That's not efficiency. That's just enough runs from enough chances to survive an ugly afternoon at Oracle Park. The win streak reaches six games because they keep finding one swing when one swing is all the math allows. Three straight one-run wins now. That margin gets thinner.",
